# Cookie & tracking check: http://localhost:8722/ ("Dobrý e-shop"; site mode; target country: CZ)

**Summary:** I ran the three-state crawl (no interaction, "reject all", "accept all"), visited `/page2.html` and `/cookies.html` after each choice, and read the page source and cookie policy. **I found no presumptive violations.** Nothing was set or requested before a choice. After "Odmítnout vše" only the consent cookie remained. Google Analytics loaded only after "Přijmout vše". The page source points to three gaps. Withdrawing consent does not delete the `_ga` cookies or stop GA on the open page. The settings layer has no button to save a choice. The cookie policy is very thin compared with what the site actually sets.

**Tested:** 2026-11-08, Chromium via Playwright, locale `cs-CZ`, crawler 0.1.0. Pages: `/`, `/page2.html`, `/cookies.html`. Evidence is in `/tmp/gdpreu-localhost-8722/` (`evidence.json`, `summary.md`, `initial.png`).
**Limits:** This is a local dev instance, so production may behave differently (CDN, tag manager config, A/B tests, geo-targeting). The crawler did not test withdrawing after accepting, the granular settings layer, or GPC; the findings on those come from reading the source. Banner clicking is heuristic. Tracker lists can miss things.

## Presumptive violations
None found by these checks.

## Warnings
| ID | Finding | Evidence | Suggested fix |
|---|---|---|---|
| L14 / GDPR art. 7(3) | Withdrawing consent doesn't take effect. If you click "Odmítnout vše" after accepting, the code only rewrites `cc_cookie=none` and hides the banner. It doesn't delete `_ga` / `_ga_GOOD1` (400 days), doesn't call `gtag('consent','update',{…:'denied'})`, and gtag.js keeps running on the open page. ÚOOÚ lists impossible withdrawal and a banner that ignores the user's choice as typical violations. Read from source only, so confirm it live. | `/` and `/page2.html` inline script: `function decide(v){ document.cookie='cc_cookie='+v…; if(v==='all') loadTrackers(); }`. There is no `else` branch. | In `decide('none')`: call `gtag('consent','update',{ad_storage:'denied',analytics_storage:'denied',ad_user_data:'denied',ad_personalization:'denied'})`, expire `_ga` and every `_ga_*` (`max-age=0; path=/`, plus the domain variant on production), and ideally reload the page. |
| L9 | The settings layer can't be used. "Nastavení" opens the "Nezbytné" and "Analytické" checkboxes, but there's no "Uložit volbu" button, so a granular choice can't be submitted. The checkbox isn't wired to anything. | `<div id="opts">…<input type="checkbox"> Analytické</div>` has no submit control. | Add a "Uložit výběr" button that saves the per-category choice and runs `loadTrackers()` only when "Analytické" is ticked. |
| L16 | The banner mentions categories the site doesn't have. It says "analytické **a marketingové** cookies", but there's no marketing toggle and no marketing tracker was seen. | Banner text vs toggles `nezbytné`, `analytické`. | Remove "marketingové", or add the category with its own toggle. |
| L16 | The policy is incomplete compared with what was observed. It doesn't list `_ga_GOOD1`, doesn't name Google as a recipient, and doesn't mention transfer to the USA. It gives `_ga` a lifetime of "2 roky", but the observed lifetime is 400 days (Chrome caps it, while the code requests 2 years). | `/cookies.html`: "cc_cookie – uložení volby, 6 měsíců. _ga – Google Analytics, 2 roky, jen se souhlasem." | Add every cookie (`_ga`, `_ga_<ID>`, `cc_cookie`) with its purpose, the real lifetime, the provider (Google Ireland / Google LLC) and the transfer basis. Also add controller details (GDPR art. 13). |
| L14 | The cookie policy page has no "Nastavení cookies" link. | `/cookies.html` has no footer. | Add the same footer link there, since the policy page is where people go to change their choice. |
| L21 | `_ga` and `_ga_GOOD1` are set without the `Secure` flag. This is not significant on localhost. | Inventory below. | Check the cookie flags on production over HTTPS. |

